          %h2#references References
          %p Standard references are
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/EGA+IV"}> EGA IV
                , section 21
            %li
              %p
                %span.newWikiWord>
                  Burt Tataro
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Burt+Tataro"} ?
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Group Cohomology and Algebraic Cycles
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139059480"} doi:10.1017/CBO9781139059480
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://ndl.ethernet.edu.et/bitstream/123456789/33006/1/6.pdf.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stacks+Project"}> Stacks Project
                ,
                %a{:href => "http://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02QQ"} 02QQ
          %p
            On the relation with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weil+cohomology+theories"} Weil cohomology theories
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            = succeed "," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                Beilinson-Lichtenbaum conjectures
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Beilinson-Lichtenbaum+conjectures"} ?
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivic+cohomology"} motivic cohomology
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marc+Levine"}> Marc Levine
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algebraic cycle complexes
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://www.uni-due.de/~bm0032/publ/CycleComplexes.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            A relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/iterated+integrals"} iterated integrals
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+spaces"} diffeological spaces
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Hain"}> Richard Hain
              ,
              %em Iterated Integrals and Algebraic Cycles: Examples and Prospects
              (
